  <p class="eyebrow">EDI and healthcare flat files</p>
  <h1>Understand the finding.<br>Fix the source.</h1>
  <p class="intro">edilint checks X12, HL7v2, EDIFACT, delimited, and fixed-width files for envelope defects and file hygiene problems. Each rule below explains what it catches, how to repair it, and when to adjust the check.</p>
  <pre>go install github.com/crb2nu/edilint/cmd/edilint@latest
edilint your-file.x12</pre>
  <p>The CLI runs locally with no network calls or telemetry. A clean file produces no output. This reference describes the current main branch; older releases may contain fewer rules. See the <a href="https://github.com/crb2nu/edilint#scope">scope and limits</a>.</p>
  <h2 id="rules">Rule catalog <span class="count">{{len .}} rules</span></h2>
  <p>Find the <code>EL####</code> identifier from your diagnostic. Use your browser's find command to search by identifier, name, or format.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Rule</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Applies to</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{{range .}}
    <tr><td><a href="rules/{{.ID}}.html">{{.ID}}</a><br><code>{{.Name}}</code></td><td>{{.Severity}}</td><td>{{.Formats}}</td></tr>{{end}}
  </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h2>Adopt checks gradually</h2>
  <p>Use <code>--disable EL3006</code> for a rule that does not fit your feed. Use <code>--write-baseline</code> and <code>--baseline</code> to accept existing findings while catching new ones. Per-rule pages explain the tradeoffs; the <a href="https://github.com/crb2nu/edilint#configuration-file">configuration guide</a> covers severity overrides and file settings.</p>
</main>
